  "notes": [
    "Attribution, measured rather than assumed. The nine metrics here move by exactly the same amounts with the god systems installed and with them removed from the scenario's deps — checked by building the reference universe both ways against the superseded baseline. So none of this delta is god-agency's: for a passive-control sweep the god does nothing and the universe is unchanged, which is what 'the verbs are the player's' has to mean.",
    "The delta belongs to 512ef00, 'Bound the frontier scan by legality, not by a range of interned node ids', which merged into this branch's base at 3894bde without a regenerated baseline. That change made roughly a third of the v1 catalogue reachable again, and referenceNodesGained and referenceNodesKnown both rise by 7.455 nodes — one number, because every node gained in a 60-tick run is a node newly known. referenceGrimoires falls 7.07 and referenceKnowledgeInstances rises 20.07 for the same reason: mages spread across a wider frontier, so more heads hold more distinct nodes and fewer months go into writing any one of them down.",
    "Still a degenerate universe, and still not a balance claim. release-plan.md forbids one before 0.5.0 and this build is 0.3.0. Every god-agency magnitude carries tuningStatus: untuned, and this sweep runs passive-control for 60 ticks — so the god holds sixteen verbs and uses none of them, no universe here ever reaches worship tier 1, and nothing terminates. What is gated is the reference scenario's vital signs, not §7's metrics."
  ],
